Data licensing for lexsync
==========================

The lexsync *source code* is released under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
The *lexical corpora* that lexsync bundles or fetches are independent works
with their own terms, summarised here and documented per corpus, with full
citations and retrieval dates, in 'corpora/ATTRIBUTION.md'.

Bundled derivatives
-------------------
The small example slices shipped inside the packages
('R_workflow/inst/extdata/' and 'python_workflow/src/lexsync/data/') and the
fuller derived corpora under 'corpora/derived/' are derived from the SUBTLEX
word-frequency family (e.g. SUBTLEX-UK, SUBTLEX-ESP). These resources are made
freely available by their authors for any purpose, subject to attribution, on
terms the authors describe as equivalent to the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike licence; the openlexicon project redistributes them
under 'CC BY-SA 4.0'. Accordingly, the bundled derivatives in this repository
are distributed under:

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

You must (a) give appropriate credit to the original corpus authors (see
'corpora/ATTRIBUTION.md'), (b) indicate if changes were made (lexsync
standardises columns and computes derived variables) and (c) distribute any
adaptations under the same licence.

Fetched corpora
---------------
Corpora retrieved on demand via the registry ('corpora/registry.yaml') are not
redistributed in this repository. Each carries its own licence and citation,
recorded in the registry and written to 'corpora/ATTRIBUTION.md' at fetch time.
Frequencies obtained through the optional 'wordfreq' connector derive from a
package whose code is MIT-licensed but whose aggregated data has mixed
provenance; consult the wordfreq documentation before redistribution.
